Another neat idea (that neither I nor anyone else will ever 
implement):

How about adding a collapsing room trap.  This is a trap which
is created with a gem on top of it (a valuable one).  When you 
take the gem, boulders fall from the ceiling, and fill up the 
whole room.  One lands on top of you, doing lots of damage.

Also, you may also have trouble getting out of the room.  If
you didn't have a way of teleporting, or some way of digging, 
you'd have to drop most of your stuff to squeeze through the
boulders.

There is a way to safely get the gem:  Just before you take it,
you drop somehting of equal weight on top of it.  Then in the 
next move you take the gem.  Just like Raiders of the Lost Ark,
where Indiana Jones puts the bag of sand where the gem is 
(except it didn't work for him, and the cave collapsed anyways).

Maybe it could have something more useful than a gem on it.

Any suggestions for improvements?
